<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan devalues rupee 3.79 pct against dollar.</title>
<headline>Pakistan devalues rupee 3.79 pct against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan on Tuesday devalued the rupee 3.79 percent to 36.9700/37.1549 to the dollar from 35.6200/35.7981 fixed on August 29, the bank said.  </p>
<p>The bank gave no reason for the depreciation.</p>
<p>One banker working in a foreign bank said the rupee was adjusted lower without any reason despite an official denial a few days ago.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
